{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For My sake.</b> For how could [He] profane [it]?—a nifal from a doubled-root [verb], and the yod in למעני is like [the yod in] ונשאר אני (Ezekiel 9:8) and [the yod in] הנני יוסיף על ימיך (Isaiah 38:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The word יחל is ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally as 'profane,' though the logic connecting it to the doubled-root (כפל) analysis and to the pronominal yod of למעני remains compressed and is not elaborated by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:34.385454723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}